// t_61109061 OVERLOAD IDENTITY.  The semantic belongs to the declaration a
// call RESOLVED TO, so overload identity must be exact.  A field-by-field
// TypeNode comparison merges `float[2]` with `float4[2]` - an ARRAY carries its
// real type in elementType, and the two agree on baseType, vectorSize,
// matrixRows/Cols and arraySize, differing only underneath.  That merge made
// the semantic of one overload apply to a call that resolved to the other,
// measured as BOTH a new over-refusal and a missed refusal.  CgType::equals is
// the tree-walking identity the analyser already uses.
//
// the UNCALLED overload carries the semantic - refusing this is an OVER-refusal
// Compile with -e beta.  Reference verdict: ACCEPT
float4 f(float a[2]) : COLOR { return float4(a[0],a[1],0,1); }
float4 f(float4 a[2]) { return a[0]+a[1]; }
float4 beta(float4 t : TEXCOORD0) : COLOR { float4 a[2]; a[0]=t; a[1]=t; return f(a); }
